cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "recount: gain-loss-duplication ancestral-genome reconstruction with arbitrary observation threshold"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Szöllősi"
    given-names: "Gergely J."
    affiliation: "Okinawa Institute of Science and Technology Graduate University"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8556-845X"
  - family-names: "Williams"
    given-names: "Tom A."
    affiliation: "University of Bath"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1072-0223"
version: "0.1.3"
date-released: "2026-05-29"
url: "https://github.com/ssolo/recount-public"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ssolo/recount-public"
license: Apache-2.0
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.20388465
    description: "Concept DOI (resolves to the latest version on Zenodo)"
keywords:
  - phylogenetics
  - gene family evolution
  - gain-loss-duplication
  - ancestral genome reconstruction
  - archaea
  - LACA
abstract: >-
  recount is a C / Python implementation of the gain-loss-duplication
  (GLD) likelihood framework of Csurös (PNAS 2026), with native arbitrary
  observation-threshold (Ωmin) support, a tree-Brownian autocorrelated
  log-rate prior (Thorne-Kishino-Painter), and a soft-landing fitting
  pipeline (Phase-0 global γ, λ + per-branch lengths, then σ-annealed
  Brownian-MAP phases) that escapes the cold-start degenerate basin on
  large or noisy datasets. This software accompanies a PNAS Letter
  (Szöllősi & Williams, 2026) that re-analyses the published archaeal
  dataset across observation thresholds.

  This v0.1.2 snapshot is a code-and-data-only release: explanatory
  notes, supplementary PDFs, and rendered figure files are excluded
  per PNAS' submission-link policy (the same code, the same canonical
  inputs, all of the validation and benchmark scripts).
references:
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: "Csűrös"
        given-names: "Miklós"
    title: "Count: evolutionary analysis of phylogenetic profiles with parsimony and likelihood"
    journal: "Bioinformatics"
    year: 2010
    volume: 26
    issue: 15
    start: 1910
    end: 1912
    doi: "10.1093/bioinformatics/btq315"
    notes: "Original Count software paper; recount re-implements the GLD likelihood and gradient algorithms developed in this and subsequent Csűrös papers."
